# The virgl Gallium driver, for guests running under qemu with
# virglrenderer. This lives here rather than in a per-flavour file on
# purpose: files like package.use.hwaccel are only applied by explicit
# per-flavour branches, and that mapping is duplicated in
# gentoo-build/emerge.sh and in image-builder. When the two drift nothing
# errors - the rootfs just silently gets different USE flags, which is how
# mesa ended up swrast-only in a disk image whose stage4 had virgl.
# package.use is copied unconditionally by both, so it cannot be forgotten.
# On real hardware this costs a few MB of unused driver, and means a
# hardware image also boots usefully under qemu.
media-libs/mesa video_cards_virgl
# libseat's logind backend only hands out a session on a console attached to
# seat0, which a serial console is not; builtin lets a root compositor open
# the DRM device directly. Wanted on hardware too, for serial-console debug.
sys-auth/seatd builtin
